  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will provide mainly dry weather to the area. A few \npassing disturbances will trigger isolated to scattered convection \nSaturday and Sunday, but most areas should remain dry. At this \npoint, storms over the weekend are not looking to be severe. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nFocus then shifts towards early next week, in which a series of \nconvective disturbances look to form to our north and west and drop \nsoutheast into our area. These could bring a damaging wind and heavy \nrain threat to our region with moderate instability and increasing \nshear expected, but overall, the exact details are uncertain at this \npoint.",
